Embedded React: a container that paints nothing is not a foreign footprint.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/scene/compositor.c and
engine/tests/scroll/test_scroll_copy.c. Proposed upstream as commit e56b83e of
pull request #293, which also carries embeddedReact-scroll-copy.patch.

Scroll by copy repaints every node outside the scrolled subtree whose last
paint reaches into the viewport, where it is and where the move carried its
pixels. That footprint is the node's box, so a container with no background,
border or effect counted too, although it has no pixels there: its children
are checked on their own. A horizontal rail whose negative margin let the
section header's transparent box overlap its top six rows added that strip at
full width twice per frame, and the damage set grew it into a repaint of the
whole rail. On the PS5 each frame of a rail scroll then took 23 ms (12.5 ms of
raster, 17 image draws, 670 kpx uploaded) instead of a strip. A plain
container with no background and no border is now skipped as a foreign
footprint. test_scroll_copy adds a paint-free header overlapping the viewport:
a 6 px scroll paints about 2000 pixels instead of about 4900, and the frame
still matches a full repaint.

